# Builder `localStorage` (presets / persistence)

## Keys

- **`section-grid-builder`** — Zustand `persist` payload for the canvas document (`persist` name in `src/store.ts`).
- **`section-grid-generator.active-tab`** — Last rail tab (`grid` | `components` | `presets`) in `src/app/App.tsx`.

## Envelope vs document snapshot

- `localStorage.getItem("section-grid-builder")` is JSON with shape like `{ "state": { ... }, "version": 2 }`.
- The inner **`state`** object matches `partialize`: `gridConfig`, `instances`, `nextInstanceIndex`, `selectedInstanceId`, `canvasPan`.
- **Built-in presets** in `src/presets/builtinPresets.ts` store the **inner** snapshot only (not the envelope).
- Apply snapshots with **`mergePersistedDocument`** / **`applyBuilderDocumentSnapshot`** (`src/storePersist.ts`, `src/store.ts`) so instances and grid are sanitized and the grid is regenerated from `gridConfig`.

## Dev-only programmatic read (browser)

In **`import.meta.env.DEV`**, `src/main.tsx` sets:

- **`window.__SECTION_GRID_BUILDER_DEV__.getPersistRaw()`** — raw string from `section-grid-builder`
- **`window.__SECTION_GRID_BUILDER_DEV__.getPersistState()`** — parsed inner `state`, or `null`

Use this to copy the current document into a new preset entry or regression test. Typings: `src/vite-env.d.ts`.

## Cursor IDE Browser MCP

Browser automation tools navigate and interact with the DOM; they **do not** execute arbitrary page JavaScript. To read `localStorage`, use DevTools, the dev global above, or paste the JSON into chat.
